  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The triangle – pass across and shot",
  "description": "One line in each corner at one end and a cone on each side further out. A runs down along the boards and rounds the cone. At the same time B takes a few steps out along the boards on the other side. C, next in line A, plays a long pass across to B. B plays it first time to A in the slot and A shoots first time. B then carries on round their cone the same way, and the next player in line B plays the long pass.\n\nRotation: after the shot, join the other line. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed in the runs."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Flat passes without bounce – take extra care with the long one."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Timing: B plays the ball in as A arrives in the slot."
    }
  ],
